  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 13, 'Transitional approach to adopting globally unique trade item numbers'. A national product code record — NPC01101001, Lamivudine 50 mg tablet, dosage form TA, route oral — branches into two tables of trade items mapped to it. The first holds GS1 GTINs (for example 58904093825793) for manufacturer MFR001 from IN, with child GTINs, child quantities of 100 and 10, 3000 eaches and a shelf life of 670. The second holds items from MFR002 from KE that have no GTIN yet and are identified only by country trade item identifiers (P006008, P006009), with child quantities of 120 and 30, 7200 eaches and a shelf life of 1095. So a national code can carry GTIN-identified and not-yet-GTIN-identified items side by side during the transition.",
      "state": "draft",
